; An edge which starts and ends at the same vertex. Both of its ends resolve, so
; the reference is not what is wrong with it: an edge of one vertex has no
; length and no direction, and a loop traversed through it would arrive back
; where it started without having gone anywhere.
(vertex geom:V-01 (frame frame:building))

(vertex geom:V-02 (frame frame:building))

(edge geom:E-01 (label "The wall which is a point") (frame frame:building) (vertices geom:V-01 geom:V-01))

; The edge beside it names two different vertices, so the rule is about the pair
; and not about the form.
(edge geom:E-02 (frame frame:building) (vertices geom:V-01 geom:V-02))
